---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Support — Milton"
  description="How to reach Milton's support, what to include, and how to delete your account."
  legal
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@meetmilton.com">support@meetmilton.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <p>
    The email address you sign in to Milton with, which AI you use and how it
    connects (for example Claude, ChatGPT, Claude Code or Cursor), what you did,
    and what happened, with any error code or message the AI showed you. Leave
    out passwords, connection keys and the text of your memos; we never need
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/setup">Setup</a> covers connecting each AI, and the{" "}
    <a href="/tools">tool reference</a> lists Milton’s two tools and their
    errors. If your AI says Milton is unavailable or a save is uncertain, open
    your TPS page in the <a href="https://app.meetmilton.com/">Milton app</a> to
    see whether the memo is there.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Choose Delete account in the Milton app, or email us from the address you
    sign in with and we will delete it for you. Deletion ends any subscription
    immediately, with no refund. What is removed and the few records that stay
    are in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>. To keep your writing
    first, download TPS.md from the app.
  </p>
</SiteLayout>
